@startuml
title SD02 - CLI text command and shared simulation (UC02; F01, F04, F09)
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 48
actor Player as human
participant Main as main
boundary "cli : CliView" as cli
control "controller : ApplicationController" as controller
participant "agent : VoiceCommandAgent" as agent
participant "model : OpenJevAdapter" as model
participant "Local SemIf / Qwen3.5 4B" as service <<external HTTP>>
control "controls : ControlManager" as controls
participant "executor : ActionExecutor" as executor
participant "up : KeyDownCommand" as up
entity "game : GameModel" as game

human -> main : main(["--cli"])
main -> main : runCli(configuration)
main -> cli : open(configuration.quietCli)
cli --> main : owned CliView
note over main, cli
  Static open selects a JLine editor with a fixed status panel on a supported terminal.
  Quiet mode, redirected streams or unsupported terminals use plain output, no periodic maps.
end note
note over main, controller : Main composes the same Java core, with CliView and no microphone service.
main -> cli : setSessionDescription(configuration.decisionDescription)
main -> cli : showHelp()
main ->> controller : start()
controller -> game : addObserver(controller)
controller -> game : addObserver(cli)
controller -> controller : publish()
controller -> game : getSnapshot()
game --> controller : initial snapshot
controller -> cli : render(snapshot)

main -> cli : readCommand()
human -> cli : type "up" and press Enter
cli --> main : "up"
main ->> controller : submitTextCommand("up")
controller -> controller : submit("up", ++utterance)
controller -> cli : showTranscript("up")
controller -> controls : beginInput(++version)
controller -> controls : getContext()
controls --> controller : context
controller ->> agent : interpret(update, context)
agent ->> model : decide(update, baseContext)
model ->> service : POST /decide\ncontrol state and bounded choices
service --> model : {backend: "semif", model, choice: "PRESS_UP"}
model --> agent : validated candidate ActionDecision
agent -->> controller : completion with locally stamped request metadata
controller -> controller : handleDecision(decision)
controller -> controls : accept(decision)
controls -> controls : validate(decision)
note right of controls
  Example assumes ACTIVE and no held input.
  Epoch, latest version and revision must match;
  action schema must be valid before planning.
end note
controls -> controls : plan(decision)
controls --> controls : new KeyDownCommand(UP)
controls -> executor : cancelAll()
controls -> executor : execute(commands)
executor -> up : execute(game)
up -> game : press(UP)
note right of controls : Remember resolved movement and accepted text; increment revision.
controls --> controller : true
controller -> cli : showMessage("Accepted: PRESS [UP]")
controller -> controller : publish()
controller -> game : getSnapshot()
game --> controller : snapshot
controller -> cli : render(snapshot)

main -> cli : readCommand()
loop scheduled simulation continues while Main waits in readCommand()
  controller -> controller : advance(seconds)
  controller -> controls : advance(seconds)
  controls -> executor : advance(seconds)
  executor --> controls : whether a timed action expired
  controller -> game : update(seconds)
  ref over game : Player.update delegates movement/lifecycle to PlayerState (SD05).
  game -> game : getSnapshot()
  game -> game : notifyObservers(GameEvent(STATE_CHANGED, snapshot))
  game -> controller : onGameEvent(event)
  game -> cli : onGameEvent(event)
  opt supported live terminal and one-second display interval elapsed
    cli -> cli : render(event.snapshot)
    cli -> cli : refreshDashboard()
    cli -> cli : updateDashboard()
    cli --> human : replace bounded status panel; preserve editable command
  end
end
note right of cli
  JLine serializes panel refresh and line editing with its editor lock.
  Resize fits the panel to current dimensions before redisplay.
  Between reads, latest state waits for the next editor initialization.
  Plain output still prints explicit snapshots and lifecycle events.
end note

cli --> main : "/quit" or null (EOF)
main -> controller : close()
main -> cli : close()
note over main, cli : Controller closes first; terminal cleanup restores its scrolling region and mode.

note over main, game
  A text line gets a new utterance identity; it never calls handleTranscript().
  Main handles /state, /pause, /restart, /help and /quit; Ctrl+C returns /pause.
  Model calls are asynchronous; all game/control mutations share one application loop.
  SD01 covers failure cleanup, SD03 context/repeat, SD04 correction/timing, SD05 recovery.
  No microphone or speech recognition is needed for the CLI.
end note
@enduml
